<title>USA: Allegheny Teledyne sees Q4 gain on sale.</title>
<headline>Allegheny Teledyne sees Q4 gain on sale.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allegheny Teledyne Inc said it expects to book a gain in the 1996 fourth quarter from the $25 million sale of commercial real estate in Northridge, Calif.</p>
<p>The company did not specify the size of the gain.</p>
<p>The real estate, which includes 35 acres and a 300,000 square foot facility, was retained by the company following the sale of Teledyne Electronic Systems in January 1995.</p>
<p>The property was sold to the Krausz Cos Inc, a commercial real estate firm in San Francisco.</p>
</text>
